# Design and revise artifacts

Implementation target: activate with compatible Studio commands.

## Inputs and scope

Read the accepted brief/plan, mode, relevant references, model capabilities and design-budget admission state. For revision, require the exact base artifact version/digest, annotation-set revision, component IDs and protected scope.

## Workflow

Produce real inspectable artifacts with versioned identity and provenance. Explain significant alternatives and tradeoffs briefly. Keep display derivatives distinct from authoritative originals; isolate untrusted HTML/SVG previews.

Read the relevant revision/approval sections of `.prism-rebuild/docs/PRODUCT-AND-UX.md`; select only applicable rules. Use the advertised annotation schema and bounds. HTML/PDF annotations bind to an immutable capture and source dependency, not a changing live view.

For focused work, change the requested region/component and compare protected areas. Report spillover rather than promising identical pixels without proof. For decomposition, assign stable IDs and an acyclic versioned graph; preserve accepted independent parts and recheck the composition.

Reserve bounded design cost before controlled dispatch. Unknown charges remain unresolved until reconciled. Do not automatically repeat a paid attempt after an ambiguous timeout.

## Mode, outputs and exit

Return artifacts, version lineage, change summary, relevant evidence, costs and a decision request or recorded decision. Guided presents the concrete result for the appropriate user decision; YOLO may select within delegated scope and budget, labelled as an agent decision. Actual user decisions remain valid in either mode.

Exit when the requested design scope has an applicable decision and handoff, or an explicit blocker remains. Design-only completion does not imply implementation, accessibility conformance or human usability testing passed.
